WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:10.987
- [Interviewer] All right Scott.

00:00:10.987 --> 00:00:12.230
Scott, where are you from originally?

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:13.063
Where'd you grow up?

00:00:13.063 --> 00:00:13.896
- [Scott] Orange County, California.

00:00:13.896 --> 00:00:14.729
- [Interviewer] Orange County,

00:00:14.729 --> 00:00:16.300
and tell me about your family.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.750
You grew up with both of your parents?

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.930
- [Scott] Yeah, both my parents,

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:21.090
they divorced when I was young,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.694
my dad was a bit of a gambling addict,

00:00:24.694 --> 00:00:28.429
when I was young and my
mom was an alcoholic.

00:00:28.429 --> 00:00:29.601
- [Interviewer] Your dad
was a gambling addict?

00:00:29.601 --> 00:00:32.847
- Addict, yeah briefly and
then he was a workaholic.

00:00:32.847 --> 00:00:35.130
He was a lawyer, so,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.890
and my mom was a CPA, she
owned her own CPA firm.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.140
They both actually owned
their own firms, but...

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:42.455
- [Interviewer] And she was into drugs?

00:00:42.455 --> 00:00:44.833
- She wasn't before I was born.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.787
I think she contracted hepatitis C

00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:53.170
through birth and then she also...

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.903
she was an alcoholic through
like most of my childhood.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.463
So very, very detached, very not present.

00:01:02.727 --> 00:01:04.627
- [Interviewer] So how was your childhood?

00:01:04.627 --> 00:01:07.560
- I never went without.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.400
It wasn't too...

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.870
I can't say I was like, I
was too disenfranchised,

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:15.920
but I didn't have the
attention I probably needed

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:17.710
and craved as a child.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.700
- [Interviewer] Did you have siblings?

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.453
- I ended up, my mom got
married to a man named Dennis.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.160
Probably shouldn't say names, but...

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:27.250
Mom got married to a man,

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.310
he was a really good stepdad,

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.960
but very, very iron
fist with him, as well.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.630
He was a Marine Corps drill instructor.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.312
So there's a lot of things
that come along with that.

00:01:38.312 --> 00:01:39.895
- [Interviewer] (chuckles) Yeah.

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:42.640
- Yeah, and then I got a
lot of sisters out of that,

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.520
a lot of step-sisters.

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:47.213
I have five, no four stepsisters.

00:01:48.409 --> 00:01:50.680
- [Interviewer] What age
were you when you left home?

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:51.513
