00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:09.950
was actually on a winter
break from school,

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.660
my oldest (indistinct).

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:13.290
- [Interviewer] Are you
still using heroin today?

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.560
- Yes. Yeah.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.960
And fentanyl, but predominantly heroin.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:17.793
- [Interviewer] How old are you now?

00:02:17.793 --> 00:02:18.823
- I'm 29.

00:02:21.001 --> 00:02:22.393
- [Interviewer] What do
you do for money now?

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:25.950
- Re-acquisition of goods.

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:28.071
Well, actually re-appropriation of goods.

00:02:28.071 --> 00:02:29.100
- [Interviewer] Understood.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:29.933
- Yeah.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.843
- [Interviewer] What
do you spend on heroin?

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.773
- Gosh, say from $100 to $200.

00:02:37.773 --> 00:02:39.023
- [Interviewer] A day?

00:02:39.023 --> 00:02:39.856
- A day.

00:02:40.759 --> 00:02:42.820
- [Interviewer] Wow.
And the fentanyl, you...

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:44.315
- Well, I try not to.

00:02:44.315 --> 00:02:48.480
I do it when I'm sick or when
I can't get anything else.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:49.970
- [Interviewer] What's
the difference, basically?

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.480
- Fentanyl is a lot more dangerous.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:55.240
I noticed that it changes
people pretty drastically

00:02:55.240 --> 00:02:56.750
like people, anybody that's

00:02:56.750 --> 00:03:00.710
a daily user of fentanyl
will change. Absolutely.

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:03.300
The core parts of the
personality, core parts

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.480
